    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62735,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "<p>Well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumour (WDPMT) is a rare, benign, papillary neoplasm of mesothelial origin.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-21T18:36:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62736,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9052/0 Well-differentiated papillary mesothelioma, benign</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62737,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F10 &amp; XH67N8 Benign neoplasm of mesothelial tissue &amp; Well-differentiated papillary mesothelioma, benign</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62738,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> well-differentiated papillary mesothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62739,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62740,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Abdominal or pelvic peritoneum {22024662; 23530588; 30419426}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62741,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>WDPMT is usually an incidental finding, but rare cases can cause pain {2295052; 22024662}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62742,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients range in age from 23 to 75&nbsp;years (median: 47&nbsp;years) {30419426}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62743,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. There is no proven association with asbestos exposure {2295052; 22024662; 30171198; 15894368; 30635798}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62744,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most WDPMTs demonstrate somatic missense <em>TRAF7</em> mutations, localized in one of a few hotspots within the WD40 repeats at the C-terminus of the protein {30171198}. WDPMTs without <em>TRAF7</em> mutations instead harbour missense mutations in <em>CDC42</em> {30171198}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62745,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are usually solitary but may be multiple. They are grey to white, firm, papillary or nodular lesions, often &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;cm {22024662; 30419426}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62746,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Common patterns include papillary, tubulopapillary, adenomatoid-like areas, and branching cords. A single layer of flattened to cuboidal mesothelial cells with bland nuclei lines the papillae. Mitoses are rare and psammoma bodies are occasionally present. The main differential diagnoses include mesothelioma, which may focally have a well-differentiated papillary pattern, and serous borderline tumour. Stromal infiltration, areas of solid growth, coalescent and complex papillae, extensive pseudostratification of nuclei, nuclear enlargement, more than mild atypia, or increased mitoses are indicative of mesothelioma {30171198}.</p>\r\n<p>Whereas mesothelioma frequently demonstrates loss of nuclear BAP1 expression by immunohistochemistry, WDPMT uniformly has intact/retained nuclear expression of BAP1 {29763720; 30171198; 27813512; 29076876}. WDPMTs are positive for CK7, CK5/6, calretinin, D2-40, and HBME1. EMA and PAX8 are variably positive {30419426; 29241740}. Unlike carcinomas and ovarian serous tumours, WDPMTs are usually negative for CEA, B72.3, BerEP4, CD15 (LeuM1), ER, PR, and MOC31 {16482993; 23530588; 23020727; 16462153}. Immunohistochemistry for L1CAM is diffusely positive in this tumour, whereas it is negative in normal mesothelium and mesothelioma {29148537; 30171198}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:49:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62747,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62748,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "<p>Absence of <em>BAP1</em> mutations and <em>CDKN2A</em> (p16) homozygous deletions may be useful in the differential diagnosis with mesothelioma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-11T17:58:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62749,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> an exophytic papillary lesion lacking stromal invasion or coalescent papillae; cytologically bland and without diffuse involvement of the peritoneum.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> intact/retained nuclear BAP1 immunostaining.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:49:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62750,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:12:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62751,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "<p>This is a benign tumour {22024662}. The occasional cases that have shown an aggressive course may represent misclassified mesotheliomas.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-11T17:58:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]